  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $7$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n7=\\frac{7}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{4}$ is $\\frac{4}{3}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n7÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{7}{1}÷\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{7}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{1}\\times \\frac{4}{3}=\\frac{7\\times 4}{1\\times 3}=\\frac{28}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{28}{3}=9\\,\\text{R}1=9\\,\\frac{1}{3}\n$$",
